For each workflow, you can set an error workflow in **Workflow Settings**. It runs if an execution fails. … The error workflow must start with the [Error Trigger] … You can use the same error workflow for multiple workflows.
You can add the [Stop And Error] node to your workflow to force executions to fail under your chosen circumstances, and trigger the error workflow.
